.el .ds Aq '
.TH HAYATE 1 "2026-07-04" "hayate 6.0.0" "Hayate Manual"
.SH NAME
hayate \- Swift cross\-device file transfer
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBhayate\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Hayate sends encrypted files and directories directly across a LAN.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
Control colored output

\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: Color when stdout is a terminal; honors `NO_COLOR` / `CLICOLOR` /
`CLICOLOR_FORCE`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always emit color, even when redirected to a file or pipe
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never emit color
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
hayate\-receive(1)
Start a receiver and wait for an incoming file or directory
.TP
hayate\-send(1)
Send a file or directory to a receiver
.TP
hayate\-discover(1)
Scan the local network for active Hayate receivers
.TP
hayate\-completions(1)
Generate shell completion scripts
.TP
hayate\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  hayate receive \-\-output ./downloads
  hayate send ./photo.jpg 192.168.1.20:50001
  hayate send ./project \-\-code alpha\-bravo\-charlie\-delta
  hayate receive \-\-code alpha\-bravo\-charlie\-delta
  hayate discover \-\-timeout 5
.SH VERSION
v6.0.0
